<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="BilliesBounce-F-Theme" spTempo="160">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1945
Composer:	Charlie Parker
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	12-bar blues
Style:	Bebop
Key:	F major

“Billie’s Bounce” was composed and first recorded
by Charlie Parker in 1945 during his influential Savoy
sessions. It is a classic bebop blues in F, with a
straightforward 12-bar framework that serves as the
basis for Parker’s highly chromatic melody and
improvisation.</spComments>
